<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Metaprogramming on cesun.life</title><link>https://example.org/tags/metaprogramming/</link><description>Recent content in Metaprogramming on cesun.life</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 24 May 2021 02:08:49 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://example.org/tags/metaprogramming/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>C++ Template Metaprogramming and Type Traits</title><link>https://example.org/cpp-template-metaprogramming/</link><pubDate>Mon, 24 May 2021 02:08:49 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/cpp-template-metaprogramming/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Template metaprogramming selects types and values during translation. The standard type-traits library supplies common building blocks; &lt;code&gt;constexpr&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;if constexpr&lt;/code&gt;, and concepts express many decisions more directly than recursive class-template specializations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="traits-transforms-and-predicates"&gt;
 Traits, Transforms, and Predicates
 &lt;a href="#traits-transforms-and-predicates" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Traits conventionally expose a nested &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; or a &lt;code&gt;value&lt;/code&gt;. Standard aliases ending in &lt;code&gt;_t&lt;/code&gt; extract a type, while variable templates ending in &lt;code&gt;_v&lt;/code&gt; extract a Boolean or other value.&lt;/p&gt;


